Z||000000||AusFiero||12-17-2001||04:16 PM||||Well to finish my stage 2 scoops I need a door skin. I had one sent to me but it is the wrong side (American drivers side not Passengers). What have people got out there?  Can someone find out how much to send one to Australia. If that is too expensive I will have to get one sent to Los Angeles to come over in a friends consolidated freight on January the 20th.<P>Help Please!<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/auschristmas.gif">        <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||12-17-2001||04:49 PM||||If I'm reading this correctly you need the Left-Hand door (American Driver's Side)?  I can probably get one this week if necessary.  FedEx freight would run about $150 to Australia... probably about $65 to FedEx 3-day ship to California, or only about $35 to Ground Ship (5-Days UPS).  This is a guesstimate on shipping based on the assumption that the package would be 36"x48"x6".  With a more accurate measurement of the door size (and the package it would ship in) I can get a more precise cost.  LMK!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||AusFiero||12-17-2001||05:03 PM||||I need American passengers side Minn. The RH one. Ouch on shipping costs direct to Australia. Unfortunately it is too big for the post hey. <BR> Is looking like a hard item to come by without spending really big bucks. You have to double the American dollar value to arrive at an Australian cost.<BR>Looks like California it is.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||12-17-2001||05:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>I need American passengers side Minn. The RH one. Ouch on shipping costs direct to Australia. Unfortunately it is too big for the post hey. <BR> Is looking like a hard item to come by without spending really big bucks. You have to double the American dollar value to arrive at an Australian cost.<BR>Looks like California it is.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>AUS, I've got a gold door (from a coupe) already off a car. It is cracked where the small piece goes above the SideView mirror- an easy fix, especially for you. I can ship it out tommorrow if you want! I'll try to get it packed tonight.  Email/PM/or Post the address in Calif.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||12-17-2001||05:50 PM||||Jim, I have several of what you need -- want to arrange a drop to L.A.? -- if so, email the address to me and I'll get it out to you..... any particular color you need?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg">  <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||12-17-2001||06:02 PM||||Thanks for the offer Minn but I think I will grab one of Terry undamaged. Might as well ship a good one over. <BR>Terry. Colour doesn't matter. Just a few guidelines but. Could it be sent just bubble wrapped or minimally packed as when consolidated I will get charged by cubic size. Plus it will be packed in with a whole heap of stuff. Also it will need some type of receipt with it say US $25 as customs this end will seize it otherwise. Also it needs to be spotlessly clean or the whole consignment will get held in a customs bond store at my expense. Sorry for so many requests but it will cost me hundreds of dollars if it gets stuffed up at customs this end.<P>The address to send it too is as follows. <P>Freight Solutions<BR>Consignee: Dave Clee - Australia<BR>12955 Chadron Ave<BR>Hawhorn CA 90250<P>Phone number of the company is 310-263-7700 if any problem arises.<P>Thanks Terry. I appreciate this. Let me know how much money I need to send you and where to. Also if you happen to have an 86 GT nose, front honeycomb and lower spoiler under the car lying around how much would you want for them? <P>Cheers<BR>Jim<BR><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/auschristmas.gif">        <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
